<title>INDIA: India Hindalco 1st half 96/97 net lower.</title>
<headline>India Hindalco 1st half 96/97 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     2,035.0  vs   2,088.0</p>
<p>    Net sales		5,136.0  vs   6,131.0</p>
<p>    Share (in rupees)	 82.06 vs	86.8</p>
<p>    Other income	   1,256.0  vs     848.0</p>
<p>    Total expenditure    3,105.0  vs   3,244.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   378.0  vs     286.0</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	   2,909.0  vs   3,450.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     194.0  vs     162.0</p>
<p>    Tax			  680.0  vs   1,200.0</p>
<p>Note: Hindalco Industries Ltd said low international prices resulted in large imports putting pressure on domestic sales.</p>
<p>The firm said aluminium output in the first six months was 79,276 tonnes v 85,867 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
